            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic and ultrasound-guided transcervical evacuation of cornual ectopic pregnancy: an alternative approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>809-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Conventional treatment of cornual ectopic pregnancy carries significant morbidity and may compromise future fertility. We present a minimal access technique for the treatment of cornual ectopic pregnancies which we believe carries a reduced morbidity and may be less likely to compromise future reproductive function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
